# A result field written under an if, read through self (#125): the arm's
# pattern is carried however the field is reached.
-- source.cue --
k: "x" | "y"
-- target.cue --
a?: int32
b!: int64
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {
	if v0_0.k == "x" {a: 1}
	b: self.a + 1
}
-- out --
unknown
v1_0.b reads self.a, which is written only under v0_0.k == "x", and the checker cannot show that holds wherever v1_0.b is written; write v1_0.b under the same patterns, or self.a on every path (rule unknown-exhaustive) @ lens.cue:4:5
